 "notes": "The two lines, the objects and their depths at Eiland 4; shoreline and piers from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL). The yellow zone buoys, placed from the PDOK aerial photos (2021 and current), sit in a row about 125 m off the quay over 170 m of shore, which matches De Meerkoeten's 'ca. 175 by 125 m' zone, and the lines run 330°. The line starts lie about 35–45 m off the quay beyond the shallow shelf; the entries are put where the 330° course meets the quay (the exact stairs are not known). All positions are approximate.",
